# XSH sem_wait() and sem_trywait()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The page shares one HTML file with sem_trywait, so both functions live
# in this module. EINTR, EDEADLK and EINVAL are "may fail" errors; the
# signal test accepts EINTR or continued waiting. The timed waits are in
# the sem_clockwait module.

assertion  XSH.sem_wait.001
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       sem_wait() on a semaphore of positive value returns 0 without
           waiting and lowers the value by exactly one (value 3 leaves 2,
           value 1 leaves 0).
test       t/001-wait-positive.c

assertion  XSH.sem_wait.002
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       sem_wait() on a semaphore of value 0 does not return while no
           post is made (300 ms), and returns 0 once a sem_post() is
           made; the post is consumed (value 0 afterwards).
test       t/002-wait-blocks.c

assertion  XSH.sem_wait.003
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#ERRORS/EINTR
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       When a handler runs in a thread blocked in sem_wait() on a value
           0 semaphore, the call either returns -1 with EINTR and leaves
           the semaphore unchanged (value 0; one later post gives exactly
           one lock), or keeps waiting and returns 0 after a post.
note       The handler is installed without SA_RESTART, and must be seen
           to run (UNRESOLVED if not). A return of 0 with no post is a
           FAIL.
test       t/003-wait-signal.c

assertion  XSH.sem_wait.004
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       sem_trywait() on a semaphore of positive value returns 0 and
           lowers the value by one (value 3: two successes leave 1).
test       t/004-trywait-positive.c

assertion  XSH.sem_wait.005
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#ERRORS/EAGAIN
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       sem_trywait() on a semaphore of value 0 returns -1 with errno
           EAGAIN without waiting, each of three times, and the failed
           calls leave the state unchanged (one post then gives exactly
           one success).
test       t/005-trywait-zero.c

assertion  XSH.sem_wait.006
anchor     functions/sem_wait.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       A semaphore of value 1 used as a lock: four threads each doing
           2000 rounds of sem_wait(), a section, sem_post(), are never in
           the section together, and an update in the section is never lost.
timeout    90
test       t/006-mutual-exclusion.c
